<%# ONE APPLICATION ON ONE LINE, for the Applications summary card:
    emoji · name · branch · the inline CI meter · its clock.

    THE BRANCH IS NAMED because the line reports whichever rung restarted LAST
    (Card#latest_suite_rung), which is not always the rung the full card reports — a
    release member's full card stays on `release` while an `accepted` merge restarts its
    suite. Naming it keeps two true readings from posing as one.

    TONE CARRIES STATE, quietly: a running or failing app reads at full strength, an
    app whose latest suite settled green steps back, so the eye lands on the news.
    An app with nothing ingested gets words where the rail would be, never an empty
    rail that reads as "0 of 0 passed".

    Locals: card - Ci::AppLadder::Card %>
<% card = local_assigns.fetch(:card) %>
<% rung = card.latest_suite_rung %>
<% progress = card.latest_suite_progress %>
<% state = progress&.state || (rung ? rung.state : :none) %>
<% settled_green = state == :green && !progress&.running? %>
<% started = card.latest_suite_at %>
<% title = [card.repo,
            (rung && "#{rung.branch} suite"),
            (started && "started #{started.in_time_zone.strftime('%b %-d %-l:%M%P')}"),
            (progress && "#{progress.passed} of #{progress.total} checks passed")].compact.join(" · ") %>
<li class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2 <%= "opacity-70" if settled_green %>"
    data-test="app-summary-row"
    data-repo="<%= card.repo %>"
    data-state="<%= state %>"
    data-branch="<%= rung&.branch %>"
    data-suite-at="<%= started&.iso8601 %>"
    title="<%= title %>">
  <span class="w-4 shrink-0 text-center text-xs leading-none" aria-hidden="true"><%= app_emoji(card.repo) %></span>
  <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-[11px] font-medium <%= card.needs_attention? ? app_ladder_position_tone(card) : "text-heading" %>"
        data-test="app-summary-name"><%= card.repo %></span>
  <% if rung %>
    <%# Shown only when the CARD has room for it (a container query on the card, not a
        viewport breakpoint): at 1280px four cards leave ~260px, and the branch token
        is what would otherwise cut "turf-monster" to "turf-mo…". The branch still
        rides the row's title there. %>
    <span class="hidden shrink-0 text-[9px] uppercase tracking-wider text-muted @[19rem]:inline" data-test="app-summary-branch"><%= app_summary_branch(rung.branch) %></span>
  <% end %>
  <% if progress.present? %>
    <div class="shrink-0" data-test="app-summary-ci">
      <%= render "components/ci_progress_meter", progress: progress, label: nil,
                 test_id: "app-summary-ci-bar", inline: true, clock: true %>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <%# Same footprint as the inline meter — 6rem rail + 0.5rem gap + 2.25rem clock —
        so every row's right edge lines up. %>
    <span class="w-[8.75rem] shrink-0 rounded border border-dashed border-subtle px-1.5 py-[3px] text-center text-[9px] leading-none text-muted"
          data-test="app-summary-ci-empty">no CI ingested</span>
  <% end %>
</li>
